From 491d37facb8b5bf217cedbfd283b0df1985b510f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 15:12:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/31] a210: build: fix v7.0->v7.1 API drift

Rebasing the A210 enablement from v7.0.12 to v7.1 surfaced a few small
upstream changes:

- clk: struct clk_ops lost its .round_rate member (deprecated in 7.0,
  removed in 7.1). Two vendor clk drivers still wired .round_rate: the
  zhihe PLL (clk/zhihe/clk-pll.c) and the vendor th1520 clk
  (clk/thead/clk.c, built by CONFIG_THEAD_CLK). Convert their PLL ops to
  .determine_rate (closest-rate table lookup, now writing req->rate) and
  their divider wrappers to forward .determine_rate. The zhihe divider
  wrapper in clk-helper.c was already converted in the 7.0 work.

- net: stmmac plat_stmmacenet_data::fix_mac_speed gained a leading
  phy_interface_t argument; update dwmac-zhihe's plat_fix_mac_speed to
  match (the interface is still read from plat_dat as before).

- clk: drivers/clk/Kconfig ended up sourcing drivers/clk/thead/Kconfig
  twice - v7.1 absorbed that include upstream and the vendor import added
  it again. Drop the duplicate; keep the zhihe include.

The complete vendor-touched directory surface and the DTB build clean on
v7.1.

